------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PARITY — every web Avatar branch reproduced (no scope narrowing)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- 3 visuals in web priority order: remote image (AsyncImage; loading/loaded/failed ->
  fallback shows beneath, the native parity of the web <img> onError) -> deterministic
  2-letter initials disc -> generic glyph (SF person.fill for kind=user, drawn Helix mark
  for kind=bot).
- djb2 seed hash -> colorIndex = djb2(seed) % 8 over the Okabe-Ito CB-safe palette.
  AvatarPalette is pinned == web CHART_COLORS_CB_SAFE; count tie-tested == Color.TS.chartCategorical
  (P1/S9). djb2 + colorIndex pinned vs the web reference: "?"->2, "u-1"->4, "u-2"->7,
  "Ada Lovelace"->2, "Grace Hopper"->7, "John Doe"->0, "Cher"->1, "X"->5.
- avatarInitials: 2 words -> first letters; 1 word -> first 2 chars; empty/whitespace -> "?".
- seed precedence (userId else trimmedName else "?") and isAttributed (neutral disc for the
  truly-anonymous case, web --surface-2) ported verbatim.
- sizes xs16/sm24/md32/lg48; glyph = round(px*0.6) = 10/14/19/29; dot 6/8/10/12; shapes
  circle / rounded(8pt); optional tooltip (.help + identity); presence dot online/idle/offline
  -> statusSuccess/statusWarning/textMuted.
- i18n: avatar.unknown / avatar.statusOnline / avatar.statusIdle / avatar.statusOffline all
  resolve through the P1/S10 facade (table "Avatar"); zero English literals in Swift sources.
- P1/S8 state-holder seam (AvatarSource + AvatarModel), P1/S11 telemetry (view.opened
  surface="Avatar", once-only), P1/S9 tokens, P1/S10 i18n facade — all present and consumed.
- Accessibility: single VoiceOver element (label=identity, value=presence, .isImage trait),
  Dynamic-Type-safe initials (minimumScaleFactor), reduce-motion-gated image fade, and a
  documented WCAG AA-large ink-tone (white unless it fails 3:1 on the swatch -> dark ink on
  orange/yellow/sky-blue), an improvement over the web's fixed white (tested invariant: every
  disc meets AA large-text contrast).

States note (P4 "stale/offline"): the web Avatar is a pure presentational primitive whose only
data source is useTranslation (no query feed), so there is NO network freshness axis to render
— fabricating a stale/offline chip would be drift, not parity. The genuine states are the image
load lifecycle (loading -> fallback, loaded -> image, failed -> fallback; never a blank box) and
the online/idle/offline presence dot, all reproduced.

